# IFC/STEP files are byte-pinned test fixtures.
#
# They are TEXT by format, so git's autocrlf happily rewrites their line endings on
# checkout -- which changes their byte length and their checksum. That is not cosmetic
# here: apps/studio/test/fixtures/ifc/manifest.json pins the exact size and sha256 of
# each fixture, and ifcCorpus.test.ts verifies them, so a normalised checkout fails the
# suite. It also means the bytes a parser test reads are not the bytes the publisher
# shipped.
#
# Measured 2026-08-27: IFC4-wall-opening-window.ifc went 12,492 -> 12,689 bytes on
# checkout, exactly 197 LF->CRLF conversions.
*.ifc -text
*.ifcxml -text
*.step -text
*.stp -text
